WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.312
The access plane.

2
00:00:01.312 --> 00:00:06.437
When Active Directory retires, being
inside the network stops meaning anything.

3
00:00:06.437 --> 00:00:11.427
M-22-09 says users should log in to
applications rather than networks,

4
00:00:11.427 --> 00:00:15.169
every application should be
treated as internet-accessible,

5
00:00:15.169 --> 00:00:19.938
and multifactor authentication belongs
at the application layer, not in a VPN.

6
00:00:19.938 --> 00:00:23.736
The replacement has four
surfaces: Zero Trust as the model,

7
00:00:23.736 --> 00:00:28.483
Conditional Access deciding each
request, a secure access service edge

8
00:00:28.483 --> 00:00:33.151
replacing the VPN, and phishing-resistant
authentication as the proof.

9
00:00:33.151 --> 00:00:40.070
M-22-09 requires it for staff, contractors
and partners, and BOD 25-01 makes

10
00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:46.062
blocking legacy authentication, and
phishing-resistant MFA for all users, mandatory.

11
00:00:46.062 --> 00:00:51.162
FIDO2 keys, passkeys, Windows
Hello, and PIV or CAC cards through

12
00:00:51.162 --> 00:00:56.074
certificate-based authentication
qualify; SMS and voice don't.

13
00:00:56.074 --> 00:00:58.600
Two consequences need an executive eye.

14
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.788
First, smart-card sign-in is
anchored in Active Directory today.

15
00:01:02.788 --> 00:01:06.713
The card and PIN stay, and
validation moves to Entra ID.

16
00:01:06.713 --> 00:01:09.107
But issuance is a separate decision:

17
00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:12.699
an enterprise certificate
authority depends on AD DS,

18
00:01:12.699 --> 00:01:16.770
and Microsoft's cloud PKI covers
only Intune-managed devices,

19
00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:21.000
so issuance needs a successor
before Active Directory retires.

20
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.121
Second, privilege: every human admin
assignment becomes eligible and time-bound,

21
00:01:26.121 --> 00:01:28.720
standing credentials go through a vault,

22
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:32.312
and emergency accounts are
tested at least every 90 days.

23
00:01:32.312 --> 00:01:37.427
The CISO decides: phishing-resistant
MFA as the end state for everyone,

24
00:01:37.427 --> 00:01:43.495
with FIDO2 or certificate-based authentication
for Tier 0 administrators first,

25
00:01:43.495 --> 00:01:48.500
opening in Phase 1, and certificate
issuance moved off AD DS by Gate G4.
